[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":111},["ShallowReactive",2],{"news-detail-2026-ifa-cultural-heritage-scholarship-in-germany-fully-funded-138":3},{"news":4,"more":28},{"id":5,"slug":6,"title":7,"content":8,"authorName":9,"authorId":10,"status":11,"recommended":12,"datePosted":13,"deadline":14,"images":15,"notifiedAt":14,"notifiedBy":14,"createdAt":13,"updatedAt":21,"categories":22,"readTime":27},138,"2026-ifa-cultural-heritage-scholarship-in-germany-fully-funded-138","2026 Ifa Cultural Heritage Scholarship In Germany | Fully Funded","\u003Cp>Applications are now being accepted from all qualified and interested international candidates for the 2026 ifa Cultural Heritage Scholarship.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>ifa Cultural Heritage Scholarship Abstract\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Scholarship Host: Institut für Auslandsbeziehungen ifa\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Study Abroad: \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarship\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Study Abroad\u003C\u002Fa> || \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarship\u002Fscholarships-in-europe\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Study-In-Europe\u003C\u002Fa> \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Location: Germany\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Category: \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarships\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Scholarships\u003C\u002Fa>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Benefits: Full Scholarship\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>A net payment of EUR 1,500 \u003C\u002Fstrong>per month\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>monthly family allowances for  \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>visa costs\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>travel costs \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>health insurance\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>monthly travel pass for public transport\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>up to \u003Cstrong>EUR 500\u003C\u002Fstrong> for a language course\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Eligibility: All Countries\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Deadline: June 30, 2026\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>ifa Cultural Heritage Scholarship Benefits\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>The scholarship covers the following:\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Scholarship search platform\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>A net payment of EUR 1,500 \u003C\u002Fstrong>per month\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>monthly family allowances for family members travelling with you (EUR 250 for a spouse, EUR 250 per child)\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>visa costs\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>travel costs for the outward and return journeys (\u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.ifa.de\u002Ffileadmin\u002FContent\u002Fdocs\u002Ffoerderungen\u002FRave-Stipendium\u002FReisekosteninformationsdokument_2026_EN.pdf\">information document\u003C\u002Fa>)\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>health insurance (including family)\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>monthly travel pass for public transport in the city of residence\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>up to \u003Cstrong>EUR 500\u003C\u002Fstrong> for a language course\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Thematic focal areas for ifa Cultural Heritage Scholarship\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>The focal areas are: \u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>cultural participation\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>sustainability\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>non-discriminatory spaces\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>decolonial working methods\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Ifa Cultural Heritage Scholarship Requirements\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>To be eligible for the ifa Cultural Heritage Scholarship, applicants must satisfy the following conditions:\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Applicants must be:\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>curators\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>restorers\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>mediators\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>culture managers\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>work with cultural heritage, collections and\u002For archive records in institutional contexts\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>name a \u003Cstrong>non-commercial, physical host institution\u003C\u002Fstrong> for each stay and submit \u003Cstrong>a specific concept note drawn up jointly with the host institution \u003C\u002Fstrong>(this is decisive for the award of scholarships!\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>ifa Scholarship Required Documents\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>While applying for the 2026 ifa Scholarship, you will be required to submit the following documents;\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Complete Application Form\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Proof of non-profit status or status as a public corporation of the host institution by means of an extract from the register of associations or a comparable certificate.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Invitation letter from the host institution for the planned scholarship stay.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>A letter of reference, e. g. from a supervisor in the applicant’s home organisation\u002Fworkplace.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Employment references attesting to the applicant’s work experience.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Contact details of the host institution.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>A \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.ifa.de\u002Ffileadmin\u002FContent\u002Fdocs\u002Ffoerderungen\u002FRave-Stipendium\u002FVorhabenskizze_Maerz_2026.pdf\">concept note\u003C\u002Fa> developed jointly by the applicant and the host institution.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>How To Apply for ifa Cultural Heritage Scholarship\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>To apply for the 2026 ifa Cultural Heritage Scholarship, follow the instructions we have outlined below; \u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Read the information we have provided on this webpage and ensure your eligibility\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>All applications must be made using the online form\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>All the documents must be prepared in full before applying as temporary storage is not possible\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Applications that are incomplete, arrive late or are submitted via e-mail will not be considered\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>make arrangements with the host institution\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>look for a host institution\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>obtain evidence of the institution’s status as a non-profit organisation or corporation under public law (see below)\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>agree on the length and dates of stay\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>jointly designate a contact person and obtain their contact details\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>prepare a joint concept note (see “host institution” below)\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>optional: check whether carrying out the travel process in reverse order would enable additional insights to be gained\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>Apply here: \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.ifa.de\u002Fen\u002Ffunding\u002Frave-scholarship\u002F\">https:\u002F\u002Fwww.ifa.de\u002Fen\u002Ffunding\u002Frave-scholarship\u002F\u003C\u002Fa>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003C\u002Fp>","LINKSKOOL",16,"published",0,"2026-04-14 13:41:06",null,[16],{"fileName":17,"oldFileName":17,"type":18,"file":19,"url":20},"assets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002F2026-ifa-cultural-heritage-scholarship-in-germany-fully-funded\u002F69de35e2ddafb1.60023741_screenshot 2026-04-14 133323.png","image","","https:\u002F\u002Flinkskool.com\u002Fassets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002F2026-ifa-cultural-heritage-scholarship-in-germany-fully-funded\u002F69de35e2ddafb1.60023741_screenshot%202026-04-14%20133323.png","2026-06-24 11:55:43",[23],{"id":24,"name":25,"createdAt":26},2,"Opportunities","2026-01-07 13:35:07",3,[29,38,48,58,67,76,85,94,102],{"id":30,"slug":31,"title":32,"images":33,"datePosted":37,"authorName":9},305,"dartmouth-college-kings-scholarship-usa-2026-fully-funded-opportunity","Dartmouth College Kings Scholarship Usa 2026: Fully Funded Opportunity",[34],{"fileName":35,"oldFileName":35,"type":18,"file":19,"url":36},"assets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002Fdartmouth-college-kings-scholarship-usa-2026-fully-funded-opportunity\u002F6a3c3537be16a2.95289717_screenshot 2026-06-24 204255.png","https:\u002F\u002Flinkskool.com\u002Fassets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002Fdartmouth-college-kings-scholarship-usa-2026-fully-funded-opportunity\u002F6a3c3537be16a2.95289717_screenshot%202026-06-24%20204255.png","2026-06-24 20:51:19",{"id":39,"slug":40,"title":41,"images":42,"datePosted":46,"authorName":47},304,"mexican-government-scholarship-for-foreigners-2026-fully-funded-opportunity","Mexican Government Scholarship For Foreigners 2026: Fully Funded Opportunity",[43],{"fileName":44,"oldFileName":44,"type":18,"file":19,"url":45},"as